<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Ilercavones</h1><p class="st-meta">500 BCE – 197 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Iberian people of the lower Ebro around Tortosa, near whose town Hibera the Scipios defeated Hasdrubal Barca in 215 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Ilercavones lived around the mouth and lower course of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a>, in southern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Catalonia</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/province-of-castellon">Castellón</a>, from about the 5th century BCE. Their position on the river made them a crossroads between the Iberian peoples of the north-east and those of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of their government. Their towns included Hibera, near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tortosa">Tortosa</a>, and they lived from farming, fishing and trade along the river and coast. They minted coins with Iberian legends, and later the Roman town of Dertosa issued coins naming Hibera Iulia Ilercavonia.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 215 BCE the Scipio brothers defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasdrubal-barca">Hasdrubal Barca</a> near Hibera, securing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. The Ilercavones were pacified by 197 BCE and absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tortosa">Dertosa</a> becoming their main Roman town.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ilercavones.jpg" alt="Ilercavones" width="320" height="305"><figcaption>Image: Ángel M. Felicísimo · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:019,445_P%C3%A1tera_del_lobo_(50053318703).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 BCE – 197 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Iberian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Iberian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ilercaones</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-348&amp;focus=ilercavones" aria-label="Ilercavones on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4612 758 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ilercavones lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5031 967h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4932 1014h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4932 1014h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Spain. <a href="/atlas?year=-348&amp;focus=ilercavones">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
